3. San Check — What am I AFRAID of? (= my avoidance bias)
4. Si Check — What am I NOT questioning? (= my blind spot)
5. Body Signal — Top 3 recs: chest open (go) or stomach tight (stop)?
6. Bayesian Anchor — Prior belief BEFORE this analysis? Actually changed?

#### 10-Breath Protocol (Minimum — No Meditation Required)
Breaths 1-3: Vagus nerve activation (4s in, 4s hold, 6s out) → DMN quiets
Breaths 4-6: Label tham/san/si voices separately → see noise clearly
Breaths 7-9: Re-ask decision question → listen to body + images
Breath 10: Say first word that appears → record → compare to logic later

#### Post-Meditation Decision Window (TOP 1 decision only)
1. Meditate 20+ min
2. Ask 1 question (the single most important decision)
3. Listen 2-5 min: body sensations, images, words, emotions
4. Record raw signal BEFORE opening laptop
5. Cross-reference with analysis after 1 hour
6. If signal CONFLICTS with data → need MORE data, not less meditation

